and <B>U.S. Bank Trust Company, National Association</B>, as administrative agent, collateral agent and security trustee for the Purchasers (in such capacities, the &#8220;<U>Agent</U>&#8221;). Capitalized terms used herein are defined in <U>Article
I</U> below. </P> <P STYLE="margin-top:24pt; margin-bottom:0pt; font-size:10pt; font-family:Times New Roman" ALIGN="center"><B><U>RECITALS </U></B></P>
<P STYLE="margin-top:12pt; margin-bottom:0pt; text-indent:4%; font-size:10pt; font-family:Times New Roman" ALIGN="justify">WHEREAS, pursuant to the Contribution, Purchase and Sale Agreement, DST Issuer desires to purchase the Transferred Assets;
</P> <P STYLE="margin-top:12pt; margin-bottom:0pt; text-indent:4%; font-size:10pt; font-family:Times New Roman" ALIGN="justify">WHEREAS, Issuers have requested that the Purchasers purchase senior secured notes in an aggregate initial principal
amount of up to three-hundred and fifty million Dollars ($350,000,000.00); </P> <P STYLE="margin-top:12pt; margin-bottom:0pt; text-indent:4%; font-size:10pt; font-family:Times New Roman" ALIGN="justify">WHEREAS, DST Issuer intends to use the
proceeds of the sale of the Notes to purchase all or a portion of the Transferred Assets from the Seller pursuant to the Contribution, Purchase and Sale Agreement, to pay fees and expenses, and to pay amounts owing to the Agent and the Purchasers on
or around the Closing Date; </P> <P STYLE="margin-top:12pt; margin-bottom:0pt; text-indent:4%; font-size:10pt; font-family:Times New Roman" ALIGN="justify">WHEREAS, the Note Parties have agreed to secure the Obligations by granting to the Agent, for
the benefit of the Secured Parties, a first priority Lien on the Collateral; and </P> <P STYLE="margin-top:12pt; margin-bottom:0pt; text-indent:4%; font-size:10pt; font-family:Times New Roman" ALIGN="justify">WHEREAS, in connection with the
